From eb2425c488bf4b6f647d6b05cd9b9e552054bfa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 23:41:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/29] vndk.rc: force software codecs via doissM CodecFix approach
 (opt-in toggle)

restore the doissM CodecFix properties that were the default codec landscape
before they were accidentally removed (a 0016 numbering collision on Apr 11,
one day before issue #33 was reported). wire them as an opt-in toggle so the
default is all codecs at vendor defaults (full performance), and enabling
'force software codecs' sets the full CodecFix landscape:

- media.c2.hal.selection=aidl  forces the AIDL C2 HAL (system-side, where
  c2.android.* live) and hides vendor HIDL C2 HW codecs that don't match
  the GSI system image.
- omx_default_rank=0  demotes ALL OMX below C2 SW codecs (rank 0x200).
- c2inputsurface=-1  AIDL buffer-source fallback for PersistentSurface.
- ccodec=4  all C2 components at normal ranks (code default, set explicitly).

this is the approach other TrebleDroid-based ROMs (doissM's CodecFix) use and
that was working before its accidental removal. the previous rework (MediaCodecList
filter alone) changed codec selection but not the underlying HAL/rank landscape,
which is why the toggle-ON log still showed 'not a PersistentSurface' -- the
doissM properties change the landscape at a lower level (AIDL HAL + OMX demotion)
that apparently makes CameraX take a different (working) code path.

Relates-to: #33
Relates-to: #94
---
 vndk.rc | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vndk.rc b/vndk.rc
index 94c7583..c7e4cd0 100644
--- a/vndk.rc
+++ b/vndk.rc
@@ -136,3 +136,30 @@ service watchdogd-gsi /system/bin/watchdogd 10 20
 on property:persist.sys.phh.adb_secure=1
     exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh ro.adb.secure 1
     restart adbd
+
+# force software codecs: replicate doissM's CodecFix approach to make the
+# AOSP software codecs (c2.android.*) the only usable encoders/decoders.
+# this was the default codec landscape before it was accidentally removed
+# (a 0016 numbering collision on Apr 11); restoring it as an opt-in toggle.
+#
+# media.c2.hal.selection=aidl  forces the AIDL C2 HAL (system-side, where
+#   c2.android.* live) and hides vendor HIDL C2 HW codecs that don't match
+#   the GSI system image.
+# omx_default_rank=0  demotes ALL OMX (vendor HW + OMX.google SW) below
+#   C2 SW codecs (rank 0x200), so c2.android.* is preferred.
+# c2inputsurface=-1  activates the AIDL buffer-source fallback so a software
+#   encoder can still create a PersistentSurface input on vendor kernels
+#   that lack the C2 input-surface HAL.
+# ccodec=4  all C2 components at normal ranks (the code default; set
+#   explicitly to override any vendor prop that might change it).
+#
+# when the toggle is OFF (default): no properties are set, all codecs are
+# available at vendor defaults for full performance.
+#
+# uses resetprop_phh -n to patch the property area directly before media
+# services read them, matching the timing of doissM's CodecFix magisk module.
+on property:persist.sys.phh.force_sw_codecs=true
+    exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh -n debug.stagefright.c2inputsurface -1
+    exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh -n debug.stagefright.ccodec 4
+    exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh -n debug.stagefright.omx_default_rank 0
+    exec u:r:phhsu_daemon:s0 root -- /system/bin/resetprop_phh -n media.c2.hal.selection aidl
-- 
2.54.0

